      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>TEST INFORMATION</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sample Type</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Sample Quality &amp; Quantity</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Method</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Clinical Indication</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp; PERIPHERAL BLOOD EDTA</td>\n<td>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Good &amp; Sufficient</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>RT-PCR</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp;Not provided&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>RESULTS</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" align=\"center\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>BCR-ABL1 </strong><br><strong>major-p210</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BCR-ABL1/ABL1 </strong><br><strong>minor-p190</strong></td>\n<td><strong>BCR-ABL1/ABL1 </strong><br><strong>micro-p230</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Transcript Detected</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DETECTED</strong></td>\n<td>Not Detected</td>\n<td>Not Detected</td>\n<td><strong>p210 (Major)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>INTERPRETATION</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The patient is <strong>positive</strong>&nbsp;for <strong>BCR-ABL1 major-p210</strong>&nbsp;transcript.</li>\n<li>Please correlate result with complete hemogram, bone marrow analysis, clinical findings, and previous BCR-ABL1&nbsp;report (if any).&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>CLINICAL UTILITY</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This test detects BCR-ABL1 transcripts (major-p210, minor-p190&nbsp;and micro-p230).</li>\n<li>BCR-ABL1 fusions are reported in more than 90% of CML&nbsp;cases, 25-35% of adult acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) cases, and 3-5% of childhood ALL cases.</li>\n<li>Several targeted TKIs are approved by the FDA for activated BCR-ABL1, primarily in hematological cancers. These include imatinib (2001), dasatinib&nbsp;(2006), and ponatinib&nbsp;(2012) in CML and ALL, as well as nilotinib (2007) and bosutinib (2012) in CML.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>REFERENCES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>H&ouml;glund M et al. Epidemiology of chronic myeloid leukaemia: an&nbsp;update. Ann Hematol. 2015 Apr;94 Suppl 2:S241-7.</li>\n<li>Salesse S et al. BCR/ABL 1: from molecular mechanisms of leukaemia&nbsp;induction to treatment of chronic myelogenous leukaemia, Oncogene, 21 (2002), pp.&nbsp;8547&ndash;8559.</li>\n<li>Faderl S et al. The biology of chronic myeloid leukemia. New England Journal of Medicine 1999;341(3):164-72.</li>\n</ul>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
